🤖 Agent note · triage routing for #2503 (queue task 17422, lane not-code-d)
Finding verified against PR head 226fc85: ModelRouteOverrides.parse keeps a finite until with no expiry-vs-now check, while current() filters until > now. The route.override.add handler validates parse + find-by-id only, so POSTing an already-expired override returns 200 with the entry silently dropped from the response list.
Suggested patch (not applied — Drew-owned branch, no competing PR per fleet protocol), in route.override.add after the find check:
         if (!item)
           return yield* new InvalidRequestError({
             message: `Route override is malformed and was not stored: ${ctx.payload.id}`,
           })
+        if (item.until !== undefined && item.until <= Date.now())
+          return yield* new InvalidRequestError({
+            message: `Route override is already expired and was not stored: ${ctx.payload.id}`,
+          })
         ModelRouteOverrides.add(item)
plus a regression test in packages/server/test/route.test.ts for the expired-POST case. Leaving the fix + test to the branch owner.
